  "texts": {
    "preamble": "A.V.Lohidakshan vs Food Inspector on 18 March, 2016 Author: B. Kemal Pasha Bench: B.Kemal Pasha In The High Court Of Kerala At Ernakulam Present: The Honourable Mr. Justice B.Kemal Pasha Friday,The 18Th Day Of March 2016/28Th Phalguna, 1937 Crl.MC.No. 7700 of 2015 () --------------------------- St 108/2012 Of Chief Judicial Magistrate Court, Ernakulam. ........ Petitioner(S)/Accused Nos. 1 2: ---------------------------------------------------- 1. A.V.Lohidakshan, Manager, M/S.Anbiswami'S Veg.Fast Food, Door No.39/1930, M.G.Road, Ernakulam, Residing At Ambalathara House, Mattathurkunnu, Kodakara. 2. Vijayakumar N.Menon, Licensee, M/S.Anbiswami'S Veg.Fast Food, Door No.39/1930, M.G.Road, Ernakulam, Residing At Nambiakurumpath, Valanjambalam, Kochi-16. By Adv. Sri.N.A.Muraleedharan Respondent(S)/Complainant & State:",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "3. Relying on the decision reported in Pepsico India Holdings Pvt. Ltd. v. Food Inspector and another [2010(4) KLT 706(SC)], this Court in Gopalakrishnan v. Food Inspector[2013(3) KLT 455] had held that the decision in Pepsico(supra) that the provisions under Section 23(1A)(ee) and (hh) of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act are mandatory and the same are applicable to all the food items.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "3. Relying on the decision reported in Pepsico India Holdings Pvt. Ltd. v. Food Inspector and another [2010(4) KLT 706(SC)], this Court in Gopalakrishnan v. Food Inspector[2013(3) KLT 455] had held that the decision in Pepsico(supra) that the provisions under Section 23(1A)(ee) and (hh) of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act are mandatory and the same are applicable to all the food items."
  },
